# Variant Index (navigation only -- header 4.2.11)

Operator guide: `docs/actors/how_to_make_variant_indexes.md`

## When

When **creating** or **editing** a Markdown artifact that already has `lupopedia.identity` and `LUP.HEX`:

- If the body has no `## VARIANTS INDEX` heading, **append** the stub at the **end of the body**.
- If the heading already exists, do not duplicate it. You may add missing TYPE.LANG rows.

## Do not

- Modify `lupopedia.headers`, `lupopedia.identity`, `lupopedia.map`, or `lupopedia.metadata`.
- Mass-scan or rewrite the corpus. Only the file you are already writing.
- Insert into PRDs, doctrine, proposals, version changelogs, or Cursor rules:
  - `docs/prd/**`
  - `docs/doctrine/**`
  - `docs/prd_proposals/**`
  - `docs/versions/**`
  - `.cursor/**`
- Put variant tokens inside KEY / HEX / SHORT / ROOT.
- Use pipes, middle-dot, or hyphens in variant IDs.

## Variant ID grammar

```text
TYPE.NUM.LANG
```

Examples: `MUS.01.EN`, `VID.01.EN`, `WEB.01.EN`, `DOC.01.EN`.

Delimiter is `.` (dot). This is **not** `LUP.KEY`. It does not create doctrine, override PRDs, or grant authority.

## Stub to append

```markdown
## VARIANTS INDEX

Navigation-only list of TYPE.LANG variants of this artifact. Not doctrine. Does not override PRDs. Does not change header authority.

### MUSIC VARIANTS

- (none yet)

### VIDEO VARIANTS

- (none yet)

### WEB VARIANTS

- (none yet)

### DOCUMENT VARIANTS

- (none yet)

### NOTES

- Variant indexes are navigation-only.
- Do not modify lupopedia.headers, lupopedia.metadata, or lupopedia.map.
- ASCII-safe dot grammar only. No pipes. No middle-dot. No hyphens in variant IDs.
```
